A program can be told to have no Dock icon of its own (Mac Driver NoDockIcon).

Steam runs as two programs with windows: steam.exe, which only keeps a hidden
window, and steamwebhelper.exe, which draws Steam's window. Both became
regular apps, so the Dock showed two Steam icons. With
HKCU\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\<app.exe>\Mac Driver, NoDockIcon = y, the
program becomes an accessory app instead: it can still show and focus a
window (a login or update dialog keeps working) but gets no Dock icon or
menu bar of its own. Without the value nothing changes.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
index 227d68b9..6b00a1f9 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -294,6 +294,17 @@ - (void) changeEditMenuKeyEquivalentsForWindow:(NSWindow*)window
 
     - (void) transformProcessToForeground:(BOOL)activateIfTransformed
     {
+        /* Cosmos: NoDockIcon (Mac Driver option). An accessory app can still show and focus its windows (a login or
+         * update dialog keeps working) but has no Dock icon or menu bar of its own. */
+        if (no_dock_icon)
+        {
+            if ([NSApp activationPolicy] == NSApplicationActivationPolicyProhibited)
+                [NSApp setActivationPolicy:NSApplicationActivationPolicyAccessory];
+            if (activateIfTransformed)
+                [self tryToActivateIgnoringOtherApps:YES];
+            return;
+        }
+
         if ([NSApp activationPolicy] != NSApplicationActivationPolicyRegular)
         {
             NSMenu* mainMenu;
